WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:08.750
When things go wrong offshore, the radio is the most important tool on the boat, and most people have never practiced using it for real.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.550
There are three levels of urgent call.

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:18.650
Mayday means grave and imminent danger to life or to the vessel: sinking, fire, a man overboard.

4
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.650
Pan-pan means it’s urgent, but nobody’s life is in immediate danger.

5
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.550
A dead engine, drifting offshore.

6
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.625
And securité is a safety message, like a hazard to navigation.

7
00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:33.800
Now the Mayday itself.

8
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.200
Follow the script on screen.

9
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.275
Channel sixteen.

10
00:00:38.525 --> 00:00:41.325
Or press the red DSC button first.

11
00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:43.850
Say Mayday, three times.

12
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.525
Then, this is, and your boat’s name, three times.

13
00:00:47.775 --> 00:00:51.125
Your position, what’s wrong, and what help you need.

14
00:00:51.375 --> 00:00:53.375
Why position first?

15
00:00:54.375 --> 00:00:58.500
If the radio dies ten seconds in, they still know where to look.

16
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.625
Then how many people are aboard, and a description of the boat.

17
00:01:02.875 --> 00:01:05.425
And then stop talking, and listen.
